# Kubernetes logs

## Gate

Load when the user asks for logs, crash output, or previous-container history.
Prefer status/events first (`kubernetes-triage`) unless logs were explicit.

## MCP tool map

| Need | Tool |
| --- | --- |
| Pod logs | `pods_log` (`name`, optional `namespace`, `container`, `tail`, `previous`) |
| Node/system logs | `nodes_log` (`name`, `query`, optional `tailLines`) — only when node-level |

## Procedure

1. Resolve pod name + namespace (list/get). Never invent.
2. If the pod has multiple containers, name the container before fetching.
3. Call `pods_log` with a small `tail` (default 100; raise only when needed).
4. On CrashLoopBackOff or "it died," also call with `previous: true`.
5. Quote a short excerpt. Redact tokens, passwords, connection strings, and
   bearer headers. Prefer error lines over startup noise.

## Defaults

1. Prefer tail/limited lines over full history dumps.
2. Do not dump every replica — pick the failing pod from status/events.
3. Init-container failures: set `container` to the init name from `pods_get`.
4. Node logs (`nodes_log`) only for kubelet/node-level asks — not app triage.
5. Log aggregation / dashboards are out of scope — API/MCP excerpts only.
